cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "DLSS Neural Rendering on AMD RDNA2 (gfx1030): Experimental Compatibility Research"
authors:
  - name: "Sakushey"
version: "0.0.1-dev-preview"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sakushey/gfx1030-dlss-nr-research"
url: "https://github.com/Sakushey/gfx1030-dlss-nr-research"
abstract: >-
  Experimental open-source compatibility research toward running DLSS Neural
  Rendering workloads on AMD RDNA2 / gfx1030 hardware. It covers ISA
  translation, a host-side semantic emulator with an independent scalar
  reference oracle, proof-oriented validation, and bounded hardware testing.
  Phase 16BO/A8C6 has crossed the first-frame correctness boundary with a
  project-owned gfx1030 core and two distinct matched GTA neural-frame
  presentations; warm temporal stability, sustained gameplay, and performance
  remain unqualified.
keywords:
  - gfx1030
  - RDNA2
  - ROCm
  - HIP
  - GPU ISA
  - neural rendering
  - reverse engineering
  - AMDGPU
  - DLSS
  - Navi21
